This file describes some info on howto install tfem on macOS with arm64
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Status at date 06-11-2023.

See INSTALL.macos for all info on installing on macOS. This file will only
describe the peculiarities on the arm64 architecture.

All primary packages/programs needed for tfem run natively on arm64:

- Xcode (from Apple).
- Command line tools (from Apple).
- universal-ctags
- fig2dev
- ghostscript
- Nagfor for arm64 (commercial)
- gfortran
- gmsh
- Paraview

For installing the non-Apple programs use Homebrew where possible.

Use framework Accelerate as LIBBLAS. Accelerate uses the AMX modules on the Mx
processors. Multithreading BLAS is only available if multiple AMX modules
can be used.

OpenBLAS also works, but is slower. Multithreading is needed to make it
somewhat competitive to Accelerate, which makes the load on the computer
much higher.

